# Test: interface backend kernel refuses traffic control backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse `traffic control backend vpp` when
#           `interface backend` is `kernel` (by default), naming the leaf and
#           both fixes (`set traffic control backend kernel` and `set interface
#           backend vpp`)?
#           A unit test cannot prove `ze config validate` evaluates the real
#           registered traffic and interface selectors end to end.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-4 (traffic control) --
#            mismatched `traffic control backend vpp` under kernel interfaces
#            is refused with both operator fixes.
# PREVENTS: VPP traffic policers being configured on a kernel-forwarding box.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
traffic {
	control {
		backend vpp;
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=traffic control backend
expect=stdout:contains=set traffic control backend kernel
expect=stdout:contains=set interface backend vpp
